{
  "text": " done on July 26, 2023. Felix James McCool, June 14, 1912 to December 27, 1972, was the United States Marine Corps Chief Warrant Officer III. He is one of two Marines to be captured as a prisoner of war, POW, twice. The first during World War II and the second during the Korean War, spending more than six years total in captivity. McCool held the record as the longest-held Marine POW until surpassed by several other Marines during the Vietnam War. Early Life and World War II Felix J. McCool was born on June 14, 1912 in Pahac,",
